  "kind": "pose",
  "note": "Threat display: the body rears -- root lifted, thorax and head pitched nose-up, abdomen dropped -- and the front pair of legs comes up off the ground, spread wide, with the fangs opened. It goes up, holds swaying between two keys, and comes down; the hold is flat so a game can cut it at either end. Spine and head pitch are NEGATIVE here, which is nose-up: `eat` uses positive ones. A pose rather than a gait because a gait scores a held-up foot as a planted one floating; here a lifted foot is simply not standing. The middle and back feet are pulled in so the lifted body still reaches the floor with them.",
